              "ms": 8
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Explain how the presence of the inorganic molecule named in <b>(d)(i)</b> affects the ATP yield from respiration.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 3
                }
              }
            ],
            "marks": 3,
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "12.2(11)",
                "role": "primary"
              }
            ],
            "markScheme": {
              "marks": 3,
              "instruction": "<i>presence of oxygen: </i>",
              "guidance": [],
              "points": [
                {
                  "n": 1,
                  "text": "<b>1 </b> (ATP yield) increases / is high<u>er</u> <b>; </b> <b> </b> <i>plus any</i><b><i> two</i></b><i> from: </i>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 2,
                  "text": "<b>2 </b> oxygen acts as final, electron / proton, acceptor <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 3,
                  "text": "<b>3 </b> oxidative phosphorylation / chemiosmosis (occurs) <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 4,
                  "text": "<b>4 </b> energy from, reduced NAD / reduced FAD / electron transport chain <b>;</b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 5,
                  "text": "<b>5 </b> proton gradient / H<sup>+</sup> → into intermembrane space <b>; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 6,
                  "text": "<b>6 </b> ATP made in Krebs cycle <b>;</b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "er": [],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "Aerobic respiration makes use of the reduced coenzymes through oxidative phosphorylation. Fermentation regenerates NAD without obtaining the large additional ATP yield from the electron transport chain.",
                  "refs": [
                    "syllabus:12.2(11)",
                    "ms:d.ii#1"
